---
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import ChapterOrnament from './ChapterOrnament.astro';

interface Props { id: string; strictSQL: string; intro?: boolean; }
const { id, strictSQL, intro = true } = Astro.props;
const modes = [
  {
    name: 'off', title: 'Explore your data',
    description: 'Keep ordinary SQL available for exploration and data preparation. Queries through an attached semantic catalog still follow its definitions.',
    input: 'Query an attached model', check: 'Validate the model query',
    outcome: 'Return approved calculations',
    boundary: 'Direct source queries also remain available.',
  },
  {
    name: 'semantic', title: 'Compose semantic results',
    description: 'Use governed semantic blocks within ordinary SQL. Compare model revisions or reconcile results while retaining the definitions inside each block.',
    input: 'Use semantic query blocks', check: 'Validate each semantic block',
    outcome: 'Compose results with outer SQL',
    boundary: 'You own the outer calculations; they are not approved model metrics.',
  },
  {
    name: 'strict', title: 'Require the reporting rules',
    description: 'Require supported business queries to follow one model attachment’s policy. Reject direct source queries and unapproved calculations.',
    input: 'Submit a business query', check: 'Validate the query and its model',
    outcome: '',
    boundary: 'The reporting contract applies to the surrounding query too.',
  },
];
---
<section class:list={['query-modes', { 'without-intro': !intro }]} id={`query-modes-${id}`} aria-labelledby={intro ? `query-modes-heading-${id}` : undefined} aria-label={intro ? undefined : 'Connection query modes'}>
  {intro && <><ChapterOrnament section="engine-query-controls" />
  <div class="section-intro">
    <h2 id={`query-modes-heading-${id}`}>Choose how much freedom a reporting query should have.</h2>
    <p>A data team comparing definitions needs flexibility. An AI reporting application may need queries to stay within an approved model. Crossfield lets you set that policy for each DuckDB connection.</p>
  </div></>}
  <figure class="mode-diagram" aria-labelledby={`mode-diagram-caption-${id}`}>
    <div class="query-origin">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="32" height="32" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="26" height="24" rx="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="m9 11 4 4-4 4m8 0h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      <div><strong>SQL from analysts and AI agents</strong><span>Choose one mode for the connection</span></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="mode-branches" viewBox="0 0 900 42" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M450 0V18M150 42V18H750V42M450 18V42"/><path d="m145 36 5 5 5-5m290 0 5 5 5-5m290 0 5 5 5-5"/></svg>
    <div class="engine-boundary">
      <p class="engine-label">Checked inside DuckDB</p>
      <div class="mode-lanes">
        {modes.map(mode => <div class:list={['mode-lane', { 'strict-lane': mode.name === 'strict' }]} data-mode={mode.name}>
          <header><code class="mode-name">{mode.name}</code><h3>{mode.title}</h3></header>
          <p class="mode-description">{mode.description}</p>
          <ol class="mode-flow" aria-label={`${mode.name} mode query path`}>
            <li class="request-node">{mode.input}</li>
            <li class="validation-node"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 2 17 5v5c0 4-7 8-7 8S3 14 3 10V5l7-3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="m6.5 9.5 2.3 2.3 4.7-4.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>{mode.check}</li>
            <li class="result-node">{mode.name === 'strict' ? <div class="decision"><span class="allowed"><b aria-hidden="true">✓</b> Execute</span><span class="rejected"><b aria-hidden="true">×</b> Reject</span></div> : mode.outcome}</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mode-boundary">{mode.boundary}</p>
        </div>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption id={`mode-diagram-caption-${id}`}>Attached semantic definitions are validated in every mode. Both <code>off</code> and <code>semantic</code> allow ordinary SQL; <code>strict</code> adds restrictions to supported business statements. These settings apply to this connection.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="engine-advantage">
    <h3>The engine can reject a query that bypasses the reporting rules.</h3>
    <p>Crossfield uses hooks in DuckDB to check the sources and calculations a query actually resolves to. Those checks follow supported queries through aliases, CTEs and prepared statements. In strict mode, a request outside the model’s policy produces an error before execution, giving a person or AI agent a chance to repair it.</p>
    <a href="/products/crossfield/engine">Why this requires integration with DuckDB’s engine →</a>
  </div>
  <details class="mode-setup">
    <summary>Use strict mode for this example</summary>
    <p><code>USE</code> selects the default model catalog. The setting applies the reporting restrictions to this connection.</p>
    <CodeBlock code={strictSQL} title="SQL · Select the model and enable strict mode" tryable={false} />
  </details>
  <aside class="sealed-session">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 10V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="12" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M12 14v4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
    <div><h3>Keep the controls in place for an AI application.</h3><p>In an unsealed connection, users can change the mode. A trusted application can pin and seal a strict connection to an approved model so SQL cannot disable the controls or switch models. The application still manages authentication and source permissions. <a href="/products/crossfield/docs/compatibility#host-controlled-sessions">Read about host-controlled sessions.</a></p></div>
  </aside>
</section>
<style>
  .query-modes { margin-top:3.5rem; padding-top:1rem; scroll-margin-top:9rem; }
  .query-modes.without-intro { margin-top:2rem; padding-top:0; }
  .without-intro .mode-diagram { margin-top:0; }
  .section-intro { max-width:850px; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3rem); line-height:1.15; margin:0; }
  .section-intro > p { margin-top:1.25rem; color:var(--color-soil-700); font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.8; }
  h3 { font-size:1.4rem; line-height:1.3; }
  p { color:var(--color-soil-700); font-size:.9375rem; line-height:1.8; }
  a { color:var(--color-link); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:4px; }
  p code,figcaption code { font-size:.9em; }
  .mode-diagram { margin:2.5rem 0 0; min-width:0; }
  .query-origin { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:1rem; margin-inline:auto; max-width:500px; padding:1rem 1.5rem; border:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); border-radius:.4rem; background:#fffdf7; }
  .query-origin > svg { flex-shrink:0; color:var(--color-field-700); }
  .query-origin strong,.query-origin span { display:block; }
  .query-origin strong { font-size:.9375rem; font-weight:600; }
  .query-origin span { margin-top:.35rem; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.6; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  .mode-branches { display:block; width:100%; height:42px; fill:none; stroke:var(--color-field-700); stroke-width:1.5; }
  .mode-branches path { vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke; }
  .engine-boundary { border:1px solid var(--color-field-700); border-radius:.5rem; overflow:hidden; }
  .engine-label { margin:0; padding:.8rem 1.5rem; background:#f0f3e9; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); color:var(--color-field-700); font-size:.8125rem; font-weight:600; }
  .mode-lanes { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); background:#fffdf7; }
  .mode-lane { display:flex; flex-direction:column; min-width:0; padding:1.5rem; }
  .mode-lane + .mode-lane { border-left:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); }
  .strict-lane { background:#f5f6ef; }
  .mode-name { display:inline-block; padding:.25rem .6rem; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.5; border:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); border-radius:.25rem; color:var(--color-soil-900); }
  .strict-lane .mode-name { background:var(--color-field-700); border-color:var(--color-field-700); color:var(--color-cream); }
  .mode-lane h3 { margin-top:.85rem; }
  .mode-description { margin-top:.85rem; font-size:.875rem; line-height:1.75; }
  .mode-flow { display:grid; gap:1.5rem; margin:1.5rem 0 0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
  .mode-flow li { position:relative; min-height:3.5rem; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.6; padding:.65rem; border:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); border-radius:.3rem; background:#fffdf7; }
  .mode-flow li:not(:last-child)::after { content:'↓'; position:absolute; top:100%; left:calc(50% - .5rem); width:1rem; height:1.5rem; color:var(--color-field-700); font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.5rem; }
  .mode-flow .validation-node { border-color:var(--color-field-700); background:#f0f3e9; color:var(--color-field-700); font-weight:500; }
  .validation-node svg { flex-shrink:0; }
  .mode-flow .result-node { background:transparent; border:0; padding:0; }
  .decision { display:flex; justify-content:center; gap:.5rem; width:100%; }
  .decision span { flex:1; padding:.6rem .4rem; border:1px solid; border-radius:.3rem; }
  .decision b { font-size:1rem; margin-right:.2rem; }
  .allowed { color:var(--color-field-700); }
  .rejected { color:#8c3d27; background:#fbf0e9; }
  .mode-boundary { margin-top:1rem; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px dashed var(--color-soil-300); font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.7; }
  figcaption { margin-top:1rem; max-width:95ch; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  .engine-advantage { margin-top:2rem; max-width:850px; }
  .engine-advantage p { margin-top:.75rem; }
  .engine-advantage a { display:inline-block; margin-top:.75rem; font-size:.875rem; }
  .mode-setup { margin-top:1.5rem; border-block:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); padding-block:.5rem; }
  .mode-setup summary { cursor:pointer; color:var(--color-link); font-size:.9375rem; min-height:44px; align-content:center; }
  .mode-setup summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--color-link); outline-offset:4px; }
  .mode-setup p { margin:1rem 0; max-width:75ch; }
  .mode-setup :global(.code-block-wrapper) { max-width:850px; margin-bottom:1rem; }
  .mode-setup :global(.code-toolbar-button) { min-width:44px; min-height:44px; }
  .sealed-session { display:flex; align-items:start; gap:1rem; margin-top:1.5rem; padding:1.5rem; background:var(--color-soil-100); border-left:3px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .sealed-session > svg { flex-shrink:0; color:var(--color-field-700); }
  .sealed-session h3 { font-size:1.25rem; }
  .sealed-session p { margin-top:.75rem; font-size:.875rem; max-width:95ch; }
  @media(max-width:900px) {
    .mode-lanes { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .mode-lane + .mode-lane { border-left:0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); }
    .mode-branches { display:none; }
    .query-origin { margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
    .mode-flow { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:1.5rem; align-items:stretch; }
    .mode-flow li:not(:last-child)::after { content:'→'; top:calc(50% - .75rem); left:100%; width:1.5rem; }
  }
  @media(max-width:600px) {
    .query-modes { margin-top:2.5rem; }
    .query-origin { padding:1rem; gap:.75rem; }
    .mode-lane { padding:1.25rem; }
    .mode-flow { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .mode-flow li:not(:last-child)::after { content:'↓'; top:100%; left:calc(50% - .5rem); width:1rem; }
    .sealed-session { padding:1rem; gap:.75rem; }
  }
</style>
